    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0137" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/795: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation
                            (Gibson) to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="20" xml:id="d6-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-31T00:00:00+01:00">January 31,
                            1932—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received February 1—12:30 p.m.<anchor n="21"
                            xml:id="d6-f2"/>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Opening. The past months have brought to the peoples of the world a
                    realization that the time has come to scrutinize with eyes open and unafraid,
                    the relations of the states to each other and the <pb facs="0138" n="18"
                        xml:id="pg18"/> efficacy of the inter-state arrangements already existing.
                    Events have been precipitated in the realm of international treaties and
                    international cooperation which make it necessary to face facts with a sense of
                    realism and with a willingness to discard the prejudices and possibly the
                    processes of the past. With this in mind, the American delegation enters this
                    work prepared to elucidate its position now and whenever it may become
                    necessary, with the directness which the present situation requires.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d6-f1" n="20" xml:id="d6-f1-content">
                <p>Except for certain additions referred to in subsequent documents, the omitted
                    portions of this document conform with the final text of the speech as delivered
                    on February 9, <ref target="#pg25">p. 25</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f2" n="21" xml:id="d6-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram in eight sections.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
